# Same values on every deploy target (Vercel, Lovable) that builds
# from this one checked-in file, so both UIs share one API/data.
#
# VITE_API_URL/VITE_VM_API_URL hold the PRIMARY/fallback backend —
# see lib/backendFailover.ts's own top-of-file comment for the full
# mechanism. Swapped by direct request ("swap the VM backup to
# primary ... fastest, free, lowest-risk fix") after Render's
# free-tier sleep (cold starts up to ~90s after 15 idle minutes) kept
# surfacing as the likely cause of several "it's just stuck/broken"
# reports — the VM is a real, always-on server with no forced sleep,
# so putting it first removes that cold-start window for the common
# case; Render, now the fallback, still covers a genuine VM outage.
# VITE_WS_URL deliberately left pointed at Render — hooks/useWebSocket.ts
# is dead code (confirmed: not called anywhere in the app), so this
# has no live effect either way; not worth touching along with this.
